{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/877472-recreating-items-of-pop-culture-with-gadgets","id":877472,"title":"Recreating Items of pop culture with gadgets!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-29T02:12:20-07:00","id":877472,"title":"Recreating Items of pop culture with gadgets!","content":"I know there have been a few threads in the past focused on gadget creation but I love the creativity I have seen in them so I pose you all a challenge. Try to recreate items of pop culture as gadgets. I'll start since it is only fair that I present something as well.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Inspiration: Ao no exorcist / Blue exorcist<br /> <br /> To recreate the main character's weapon I feel it would in truth take two separate gadgets. The first as a blade that has been exploited with hellfire to make it a blade wreathed in blue flames while the second would be a simple sword sheath with a N.F.E. of going native to make the sword mundane until drawn from the sheath. <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Inspiration: Ghost busters<br /> <br /> For the effect of the ghost trap I feel an exploited item with solitary confinement that can only trap ephemeral beings within it would capture the concept of the ghost trap. The ability to hold multiple is probably where the gadget would deviate from its inspirations and instead only be able to hold a single entity at a time and likely also only for a limited time.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Inspiration: The matrix<br /> <br /> A knock o<span style=\"font-family:arial\">ff ga<span style=\"font-size:12px\">dget or precisionly engineered with the emb</span>ed d</span>ownload knowledge as a N.F.E. to allow one to download a fighting style at a number of dots equal to the successes on the activation for a scene (or the next scene). This would allow one to have the functionality of &quot;wow, I know kung fu&quot; without long term effects.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Inspiration: Stargate<br /> <br /> A set of doorframes exploited with the <u>same instance</u> of two places at once allowing one to walk through one and out the other when active. Though I would like this to count as a single gadget I know it is possible for it to be counted as separate gadgets. As separate gadgets however you could play truer to Stargate with a network of there gates all interlocked (despite the risks).<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Inspiration: Doctor who<br /> <br /> To recreate the perception filter of Doctor who I feel it'd be as simple as an utilizing the embed lost in the crowd. Either for an item, like the T.A.R.D.I.S., to be hidden on a busy street or a person wearing a necklace with the embed would recreate the effects shown in the show.<br /> <br /> <br /> So show me what you all can come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T05:37:10-07:00","id":877595,"title":"","content":"If I had to classify the TARDIS as a Gadget, I would make it a third tier Lambda consisting of Behind The Curtain + Four Minutes Ago + Lost In The Crowd + Deep Pockets, for moving through space, travelling through time, perception filtering and being bigger on the inside, respectively.<br /> <br /> The Omnitrix from Ben10 might consist of Living Installation + Hellhounds + Show Of Power, to bond with the user on a genetic level and transform them into many Cryptids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-29-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T06:13:02-07:00","id":877618,"title":"","content":"Zat guns from Stargate could be reflected with Knockout Punch. Possibly add Merciless Gunman for their second effect? (We don't talk about the third effect.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:40:00-07:00","id":877805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/877472-recreating-items-of-pop-culture-with-gadgets?p=877595#post877595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to classify the TARDIS as a Gadget, I would make it a third tier Lambda consisting of Behind The Curtain + Four Minutes Ago + Lost In The Crowd + Deep Pockets, for moving through space, travelling through time, perception filtering and being bigger on the inside, respectively.<br /> <br /> The Omnitrix from Ben10 might consist of Hellhounds + Show Of Power, to transform the user into many Cryptids.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice job. That said, the TARDIS is totally a Lare. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One of the four inspirations I based them on, actually.<br /> <br /> The Sonic Screwdriver is clearly a Lambda made using Right Tools, Right Job and Like The Movies, letting it do just about anything necessary for the narrative :P<br /> <br /> The Interlock Download Knowledge in the DSG is an obvious Matrix homage - one thing I wish I'd made canon in that chapter is the idea of <i>Interlock</i>-gadgets (with the caveat that you can't reverse engineer them)....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:13:09-07:00","id":877850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/877472-recreating-items-of-pop-culture-with-gadgets?p=877805#post877805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one thing I wish I'd made canon in that chapter is the idea of <i>Interlock</i>-gadgets (with the caveat that you can't reverse engineer them)....</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd thought about asking about Interlock Gadgets, but then I thought the likely response would be &quot;that's what Lambdas are for&quot;. I mean, a (Demonic) Interlock is Embed + Embed, which is a valid Lambda combination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T11:31:49-07:00","id":877921,"title":"","content":"Soul Cube from Doom 3<br /> <br /> I'd probably say this would be a second order Lambda with Ephemeral Cover + Devour Infrastructure+ Eye for an Eye, a powerful angel killing weapon that is capable of repairing and refueling it's user?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T13:27:13-07:00","id":878043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/877472-recreating-items-of-pop-culture-with-gadgets?p=877805#post877805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nice job. That said, the TARDIS is totally a Lare. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One of the four inspirations I based them on, actually.<br /> <br /> The Sonic Screwdriver is clearly a Lambda made using Right Tools, Right Job and Like The Movies, letting it do just about anything necessary for the narrative :P<br /> <br /> The Interlock Download Knowledge in the DSG is an obvious Matrix homage - one thing I wish I'd made canon in that chapter is the idea of <i>Interlock</i>-gadgets (with the caveat that you can't reverse engineer them)....</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree that the TARDIS is a Lare. It is self-aware, and it even develops a human Cover of sorts in &quot;The Doctor's Wife&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Sonic Screwdriver is a second tier Lambda consisting of Right Tools Right Job + Like I Built It + Cause And Effect. I lumped the lock-picking, repairing and disassembling into the first Embed, the various data gathering methods into the second and all the miscellaneous &quot;reverse the polarity of the neutron flow&quot; sort of technobabble into the third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:02:47-07:00","id":878131,"title":"","content":"As a side note, K-9 is a Cryptid, not a Gadget. The difference is that the Doctor has a Merit that modifies his Hellhounds Exploit. With it, he can use Crafts instead of Animal Ken, that is, build fine-tuned Cryptids as machines instead of mutating animals. Said Merit also comes with a way or another of letting the Cryptid acquire, store and use Aether, without having to rip it off Demons or other supernaturals. The Psychic Paper is just Authorized, but the Installation got an Exceptional Success, making it versatile in the credentials it can project and allowing it to fool machines.<br /> <br /> Changing the series, I'd say the Neuralizer from Men In Black is Never Here + The Only Word That Matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-01-2016, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T19:42:20-07:00","id":879854,"title":"","content":"What about the Terror Mask from Splatterhouse? I think it would consist of Merge + Hellhounds + Break To Heal. The first Exploit fuses the Mask with the wearer. The second gives natural weaponry and enhances physical traits. The third allows the wearer to harvest Aether by killing, which can then be used to power their Cryptid Adaptations/Demonic Form Advantages. Do you need to add the Living Installation Exploit to Lambda Gadgets before they can fuse with living beings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}